From 8ec0da883e93f59be737fdafc92b89d41ee43b51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:32:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 63/63] go.mod: quic-go of the podkop-engine fork, Chrome's
 QUIC suites in the order of the CPU

The ClientHello of the Chrome QUIC parrot (hysteria2, xhttp over HTTP/3) offered AES-GCM first on
every CPU; Chrome itself puts ChaCha20 first without AES hardware (BoringSSL), and a server takes
the first suite it supports: on an MT7621, hysteria2 of 1.14 moved a third less and cost 40 % more
CPU a GB than 1.13. podkop-net/quic-go v0.61.0-sing-box-mod.12-pdk.1 is upstream
v0.61.0-sing-box-mod.12 and that one change (the order of crypto/tls's hasAESGCMHardwareSupport).

Pdk-Feature: quic-chrome-suites
Pdk-Zone: build
Pdk-Layer: 05
---
 go.mod | 4 ++++
 go.sum | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/go.mod b/go.mod
index f4bf8c02e..df4b2b69e 100644
--- a/go.mod
+++ b/go.mod
@@ -200,3 +200,7 @@ require (
 )
 
 replace github.com/sagernet/sing-vmess => github.com/FiyeroT/sing-vmess v0.2.9-pdk.2
+
+// Chrome's QUIC ClientHello in the order of the CPU: ChaCha20 first without AES hardware, as Chrome
+// does (podkop-engine, K1)
+replace github.com/sagernet/quic-go => github.com/podkop-net/quic-go v0.61.0-sing-box-mod.12-pdk.1
diff --git a/go.sum b/go.sum
index 717a2152f..da8e75313 100644
